  "memory.md": "# Agent memory: Dora\n\n> **Fictional persona. Synthetic data.** This is everything the agent is allowed to remember about Dora. It stores only workout-relevant context: no event titles, locations, contacts, diagnoses or medical records.\n\n## Profile (user-provided)\n- Age range: 25–34\n- Experience: CrossFit for 6 years; competes in the RX division at local throwdowns\n- General fitness: highly trained; 5–6 sessions a week\n- Injury history: none she has reported\n- Current health status: reports feeling good (no illness or injury reported)\n- Energy (user-reported): good now; expects jet lag\n\n## Goals\n- Long-term: top 10 in the RX women's division at the Harbor Throwdown, Sat Dec 5, 2026\n- Short-term: keep the strength and engine built over the summer (back squat 225 lb, clean & jerk 165 lb, 2,000 m row 7:35) through the trip, and start the competition block on time\n\n## Plan position\n- Week 6 of 14 (Strength block). Plan page: \"Dora: Throwdown Prep (14 weeks)\"\n- Family trip: Sat Oct 10 to Fri Oct 23 (14 days). Home on the evening of Fri Oct 23, six weeks before the event.\n\n## Recurring availability (workout-relevant only)\n- At home: trains 6:00–7:15 am Mon–Fri and 8:00 am Sat; works 8:30 am–5:00 pm\n- On the trip: family plans on most days (see calendar); she says the early morning before them is hers\n\n## Equipment\n- At home: full CrossFit gym (Olympic barbells, bumper plates, rowing erg, sled, assault bike, pull-up rig, rings, kettlebells)\n- On the trip: bodyweight and one medium resistance band. Hotel gyms are not confirmed, so do not count on them.\n\n## Known preferences\n- Protects the competition goal; open to shorter sessions while away.\n- Has **not** said whether she wants to train on flight days.\n\n## Past changes made with the agent\n- None.",
  "workout-plan.md": "# Dora: Throwdown Prep (14 weeks)\n\n> **Fictional persona. Synthetic data for the Workout Program Manager capstone prototype.**\n\n## Goal\n- **Long-term goal:** Top 10 in the RX women's division at the Harbor Throwdown.\n- **Short-term goal (this block):** Hold the strength and engine built over the summer, then build competition-specific capacity from week 9.\n- **Event day:** Saturday, December 5, 2026.\n\n## Where Dora is now\n- **Current week:** Week 6 of 14 (Mon Oct 5 to Sun Oct 11, 2026), Strength block.\n- Weeks 7–8 (Oct 12–25) fall during a family trip that was booked after this plan was written.\n- **Week 9 (from Mon Oct 26)** starts the competition block, six weeks before the event.\n\n## Weekly structure\n| Day | Session | Usual time | Length | Equipment |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Mon | Olympic lifting + back squat | 6:00 am | 75 min | Barbell, bumper plates, rack |\n| Tue | Metcon + rowing intervals | 6:00 am | 60 min | Rowing erg, barbell, kettlebells |\n| Wed | Gymnastics + accessories | 6:00 am | 60 min | Pull-up rig, rings, dumbbells |\n| Thu | Heavy deadlift + press + sled | 6:00 am | 75 min | Barbell, bumper plates, sled |\n| Fri | Competition-style workout | 6:00 am | 60 min | Barbell, rowing erg, assault bike |\n| Sat | Long aerobic + skill | 8:00 am | 60 min | Rowing erg or assault bike |\n| Sun | Rest | (none) | | |\n\n## Weeks 5–10 at a glance\n| Week | Starts (Mon) | Phase | Focus |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 5 | Sep 28 | Strength | Back squat 5 × 3 at 82.5%, clean & jerk technique, 2 metcons |\n| **6** | **Oct 5** | **Strength (current)** | **Back squat 5 × 3 at 85%, deadlift 4 × 3, 2 metcons** |\n| 7 | Oct 12 | Strength | Back squat 5 × 3 at 87.5%, deadlift 4 × 3 at 85%, 2 metcons |\n| 8 | Oct 19 | Deload | All loads at 70%, skill work, 2 short metcons |\n| 9 | Oct 26 | Competition 1 | 3 competition-style workouts, heavy singles to 90% |\n| 10 | Nov 2 | Competition 2 | 3 competition-style workouts, event simulations |\n\nWeeks 11–14: competition 3, peak, taper, event week (Throwdown Sat Dec 5).\n\n## Typical sessions\n| Session | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| Olympic lifting + back squat | Snatch and clean & jerk technique (30 min), back squat 5 × 3, core |\n| Metcon + rowing intervals | 6 × 500 m row at 2,000 m pace, then a 12-min metcon (thrusters, kettlebell swings, burpees) |\n| Gymnastics + accessories | Kipping and strict pull-ups, toes-to-bar, handstand push-ups, dumbbell accessories |\n| Heavy deadlift + press + sled | Deadlift 4 × 3, push press 4 × 4, 6 × 20 m heavy sled push |\n| Competition-style workout | Barbell cycling, rowing and assault bike under time, scored |\n| Long aerobic + skill | 45 min steady row or assault bike, then 15 min skill (double-unders, muscle-ups) |\n\n## Equipment and access\n- Home gym: Ironbark CrossFit (made up). Full equipment.\n- On the trip: see memory (bodyweight and one resistance band).",
